PART 3: THE DEFAULT'S SCOPE
   (3a) two defaults for one label, pool A (21): `(h = 0: <5) & (h = 9: >7)` holds on 11 (smallest 'c'), `(h = v: <5 & >7)` on 0 for every v
   (3b) a default reaching later readers only (positional): `(a = 0: <10) & (b: >$a)` holds on 54, `(b: >$a) & (a = 0: <10)` on 45: differ 9 (`&` stops commuting)
   (3c) a default on a looped label, RZ zero-pass subjects (10): `(h = 0: <5)` holds on 10 (the LEFT JOIN row reads 0), `some((h = 0: <5))` on 0 (no pass to read); on all 1,110: 310 vs 800
   (3d) a default the label never holds, T2 `((h, m = v): late)`: v = 0 vs v = 60 (no two-digit minute field reads 60 in a time, but the regex's m is \d\d, so 60 IS a value it holds): differ 2; v = 0 vs v = "x": 90

